/T (Sport is the most popular category by both session volume \(43%\) and unique participants \(312\). Study activities show the highest sessions-per-user ratio \(1.4\), suggesting that students who use the platform for academic peer support engage repeatedly. Board Games, while the smallest category, accounts for 26% of all sessions and serves as a low-barrier entry point for students who may not be drawn to sport or formal study groups.)
/E (Sport is the most popular category by both session volume \(43%\) and unique participants \(312\). Study activities show the highest sessions-per-user ratio \(1.4\), suggesting that students who use the platform for academic peer support engage repeatedly. Board Games, while the smallest category, accounts for 26% of all sessions and serves as a low-barrier entry point for students who may not be drawn to sport or formal study groups.)
